figdown 0.1 block
# core §13.4: a document from ANY earlier version must reach the current one
# in a SINGLE run. This is written in the oldest spellings the tool still
# carries — six releases of them — and must land fully migrated after one pass.
# The `layer`/`layer=` pair stood here until 0.3; `PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT` WITHDREW their
# target, so a chain containing them no longer completes and the halt is
# pinned by its own fixture, 951-chain-halted-by-withdrawal.
node b "B" kind=decision
node c "C" kind=process
boundary e "Upstream"
edge b -> c
edge b -> e
render
pin b at=20,20
size b w=100 h=40
